# Eastron SDM120CT.
# Converted automatically from the Omni Console device library (OmniCoreST); see ATTRIBUTION.md.
# Not verified against the manufacturer's documentation.
# Corrections are welcome (CONTRIBUTING.md). Remove @x_status once this table has been checked against the manual.
# | Eastron SDM120CT — Modbus register map for Omni Console
# | 
# | Source: eastron-sdm120ct-modbus-protocol.pdf (SDM120CTM Modbus Protocol V1.3)
# | Single-phase CT-connected smart meter (external CT input, 5A secondary).
# | All measured values are IEEE-754 FLOAT (f32), MSW first (big-endian) — word_order omitted.
# | Measurements use INPUT registers (FC04). Addresses are 0-based protocol addresses.
# | Factory defaults: slave=1, baud=2400, 8N1.
# | CT-specific holding registers: CT1 (40051, primary current 5-9999A, default 5A),
# | CT2 (40053, secondary ratio: 1A or 5A, default 5A).
# | Register map identical to SDM120 except for CT configuration holding registers.
@mbmap=1
@vendor=Eastron
@model=SDM120CT
@description=Single-phase CT-connected smart meter — V/I/P/Q/S, PF, frequency, import/export energy. CT input (5A secondary). Register map identical to SDM120.
@source=Omni Console device library (OmniCoreST), modbus-library/eastron-sdm120ct.toml; Source: eastron-sdm120ct-modbus-protocol.pdf (SDM120CTM Modbus Protocol V1.3). Not verified against the manufacturer's documentation
@byte_order=ABCD
@address_base=0
@x_status=unverified
@x_origin=omniconsole

